    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d694">

                <pb facs="0831" n="757" sameAs="frus:frus1917Supp02v01/pg757"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 763.72111N39/132</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Italy</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Page</hi>)
                        <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Rome</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1917-11-30T12:00:00+01:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">November 30, 1917, noon</hi></date>. <lb/> [<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Received 4.06 p.m.</hi>]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Department’s 984, November 24, 3 p.m.<anchor n="1" xml:id="d694-f1"/> Foreign
                    Office informs me verbally, Baron Sonnino
                    to whom matter was directed, telegraphs <pb facs="0832" n="758" xml:id="pg758"/>
                    to-day from Paris that he sees no objection to United States making desired
                    declaration to Swiss Government. Foreign Office promises written
                    confirmation.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Nelson Page</hi>
                        
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d694-f1" n="1" xml:id="d694-f1-content">
                <p>See telegram No. 5895 of that date to the Ambassador in Great Britain, <hi
                        rendition="#italic">ante</hi>, <ref target="#pg756">p. 756</ref>.</p>
            </note>
